  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2501.00001v1</id>
    <title>Sparse Autoencoders &amp; Interpretability: A Practical Guide</title>
    <updated>2025-01-01T10:00:00Z</updated>
    <published>2025-01-01T10:00:00Z</published>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.00001v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.00001v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Background: sparse autoencoders have become a standard tool for mechanistic interpretability.
  Methods: we train SAEs on residual stream activations of a 7B model.
  Results: dictionary features recover 82% of the variance explained by supervised probes.
  Conclusions: SAEs are useful but require careful hyperparameter tuning.</summary>
